    {
      "id": 60741,
      "name": "Putts",
      "username": "Putts",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/c5a1d2/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-04-22T15:55:46.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I too store all of the cards unsleeved in the EE box. &nbsp;Heroes on the left, villains and environments on the right. &nbsp;The hero side is completely snug, so when I want to remove a hero deck, I just gently pull up on the two divider cards on either side of it, and the deck just lifts up with the dividers. &nbsp;Once the first deck is removed, there's enough leeway to reach my fingers in and directly grab any other deck.</p><p>I keep my oversized villain cards and the tokens in the Shattered Timelines box. &nbsp;Not the most elegant solution, but it works.</p>",
      "post_number": 14,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:36:52.155Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
